SLUG: guides/moving-checklist.html
TITLE: Moving Checklist for Kanpur — what to do, week by week
DESC: A practical house-moving checklist for Kanpur: what to sort four weeks out, two weeks out, the week before, moving day itself, and the first week in the new home.
HEADING: Moving checklist
LEAD: What to do and when, from four weeks out to your first week in the new place. Use your browser's print option to keep a paper copy — the page is formatted for it.
CRUMBS: Home|/ ; Guides|/guides/moving-checklist.html ; Moving checklist|
---

  <section class="section on-paper">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow flow">
        <p class="lead">
          Moving goes wrong in the admin, not the lifting. Most of what causes
          a bad move day — a missing gate pass, a lift that was never booked,
          an address nobody updated — is decided weeks earlier.
        </p>
        <p>
          Nothing here is specific to using us. It is the list we would give a
          friend.
        </p>
        <div class="btn-row mt-6">
          <button class="btn btn--ghost" type="button" data-print>
            <svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-download"/></svg>
            Print this checklist
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section is-tight on-sunk">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow">

        <h2>Four weeks before</h2>
        <ul class="ticks mt-5">
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Get two or three written quotes. Ask each for the same itemised breakdown so you are comparing the same job.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Fix your date — and check whether it falls in the month-end rush, when vehicles and crews are scarce and dearer.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Start decluttering. You pay to move volume, so anything you will not unpack is worth dealing with now.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Give notice to your landlord if you are renting, and confirm what the deposit return depends on.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>If children are changing school, request transfer certificates now — they take longer than people expect.</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="mt-8">Two weeks before</h2>
        <ul class="ticks mt-5">
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Confirm the booking in writing, with the vehicle size and crew size stated.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Book the service lift and a gate pass at both buildings, and check the permitted shifting hours.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Arrange transfer or final readings for electricity, water, gas, broadband and the newspaper.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Book a technician for anything that needs professional disconnection — split AC, geyser, water purifier.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Update your address on bank records, insurance, Aadhaar and any subscription that posts you something.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Use up frozen food and anything that will not travel.</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="mt-8">The week before</h2>
        <ul class="ticks mt-5">
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Pack an "open first" box: kettle, mugs, tea, phone chargers, toilet roll, soap, a towel each, basic tools, torch, bedsheets.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Set aside documents, jewellery, cash and medicines to carry yourself. These never go on the truck.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Photograph the back of your TV and router so you can reconnect the cables without guessing.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Confirm who will be present at each address, and share their numbers with your coordinator.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Arrange care for pets and small children on the day. A house full of open doors is not the place for either.</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="mt-8">The day before</h2>
        <ul class="ticks mt-5">
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Defrost and drain the fridge, and drain the washing machine hoses. Both need to be properly dry.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Have gas cylinders emptied and disconnected by the supplier — they cannot travel loaded.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Charge your phone and a power bank. You will be on calls all day.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Withdraw some cash for incidentals, and keep it on you.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Confirm the arrival time with the crew and re-check the lift booking.</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="mt-8">Moving day</h2>
        <ul class="ticks mt-5">
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Walk the crew through the house first, and point out anything fragile or already damaged.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Keep your personal bag with documents and valuables in one place, with you.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Check the inventory and sign the loading sheet before the vehicle leaves.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Walk every room, cupboard and balcony before locking up. Check the loft and behind doors.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Take meter readings and photograph them.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>At the new place, check goods against the inventory as they come off — and note anything wrong on the sheet <em>before</em> the crew leaves.</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="mt-8">First week in the new home</h2>
        <ul class="ticks mt-5">
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Test every appliance, including the ones you did not use on day one.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Get the locks changed if you have moved into a resale or previously rented property.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Register with the society office and collect any parking or access cards.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Find your nearest hospital, pharmacy and police station before you need them.</span></li>
          <li><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span>Report any damage in writing within the window your mover stated.</span></li>
        </ul>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section is-tight cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="wrap-narrow text-centre">
        <h2>Want us to handle the heavy part?</h2>
        <p class="lead">Surveyed first, quoted in writing, moved by our own crews.</p>
        <div class="btn-row mt-6 btn-row--centre">
          <a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact.html" data-open-callback>Request a callback</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/faq.html">Read the FAQ</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
